<routes xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://sumo.dlr.de/xsd/routes_file.xsd">

    <!--
      Three-car cooperative emergency braking scenario (Rolich et al.
      VTC 2024). Tuned so the algorithm actually does something visible.

      The previous version had no actionStepLength on the followers, so
      Krauss reacted to V1's brake in the same simulator step it happened
      (perception latency ≈ 0). The algorithm physically cannot beat
      zero — and so baseline and σ-sweep numbers were identical, which
      is the symptom you saw.

      Fix: actionStepLength=1.0 on middle/follower introduces a 1 s
      decision cycle. Between decisions the follower coasts at the last
      chosen speed. The algorithm's TraCI-issued slowDown bypasses the
      cycle and fires within a few ms of the DENM arrival, so

        baseline ⇒ V2 might not see V1's brake until up to 1 s later,
                   then brakes hard against a closer V1.
        algorithm ⇒ V2 brakes immediately at optimal_a2, smoothly and
                   from farther away.

      Scenario kinematics:
        cruise speed         20 m/s    (lane speed limit 25 → vType cap)
        follower decel       4 m/s²
        follower emergDecel  6 m/s²
        follower tau         0.6 s     (steady-state Krauss headway)
        action delay         1.0 s     (perception lag the algo beats)
        starting gaps        ≈ 50 m    (1.0·v_cruise + safety margin)
        forced brake at      t = 15 s, slowDown(0, 1.0)

      Expected outcomes (numerically, will vary slightly per run):
        baseline:  V2 stops ~3-5 m short of V1; HARM(t) has a spike
                   ≈ 1 s wide when V2 finally brakes hard.
        algorithm: V2 stops ~25-30 m short of V1; HARM(t) ramps
                   smoothly without the late-brake spike.
    -->

    <vType id="leader"   accel="3.0" decel="9.0" emergencyDecel="9.0"
           maxSpeed="20" minGap="0.5" tau="0.3" length="5.0" sigma="0.0"
           actionStepLength="0.1" mass="2000"
           carFollowModel="Krauss" color="1,0,0"/>

    <vType id="middle"   accel="3.0" decel="4.0" emergencyDecel="6.0"
           maxSpeed="20" minGap="0.5" tau="0.6" length="5.0" sigma="0.0"
           actionStepLength="1.0" mass="1500"
           carFollowModel="Krauss" color="1,1,0"/>

    <vType id="follower" accel="3.0" decel="4.0" emergencyDecel="3.0"
           maxSpeed="20" minGap="0.5" tau="0.6" length="5.0" sigma="0.0"
           actionStepLength="1.0" mass="1200"
           carFollowModel="Krauss" color="0,0,1"/>

    <!-- Departures spaced so steady-state Krauss headway settles to
         ~50 m between consecutive vehicles by the time V1 brakes. -->
    <vehicle id="veh0" type="leader"   depart="0.00" departSpeed="max">
        <route edges="E0"/>
    </vehicle>

    <vehicle id="veh1" type="middle"   depart="2.50" departSpeed="max">
        <route edges="E0"/>
    </vehicle>

    <vehicle id="veh2" type="follower" depart="5.00" departSpeed="max">
        <route edges="E0"/>
    </vehicle>

</routes>
